      "page": 1,
      "text": "HT-8\nEightballers\nCDR D. Burkett NAS WHITING FIELD, FL CDR S. Kohl\nCommanding Officer Executive Officer\nTraining the World's Best Helicopter Pilots\nSaturday, 21-Nov-2026\nSUNRISE: 06:20 MOONRISE: 14:30 % ILLUM: 85% JULIAN DATE: 6325\nSUNSET: 16:48 MOONSET: 02:59\nTOTAL FLY EVENTS: 4 TOTAL FLY HRS: 7.4\nTOTAL SIM EVENTS: 10 TOTAL SIM HRS: 15.0\nQuestions:\nEP Question: ROTOR BRAKE ON\nGeneral: What publications are required for flight?\nNATOPS: What is the definition of a Precautionary Emergency Landing (PEL)?\nSOP: The ______ shall be turned on no lower than the _____ on all instrument approaches.\nDUTY/WATCH ASSIGNED SIGN IN SIGN OUT\nFDO LT BOWES C 0700 0659\nDUTY DRIVER 1stLt CROUSHORN C 0730 0729\nAM SDO ENS FLOWER J 0700 1900\nPM SDO 2ndLt BUDZ P 1900 0700\n***** Notes *****\nSouth Field NO CTO: 0700 \u2013 1500\nCONTACT NORTH TOWER FOR DEPARTURE AND ARRIVAL\nCTO: 1500 \u2013 2300\n0800 - 1500\nNorth Field TWR: 0800 \u2013 1500\nCTO: 1500 \u2013 2300\nPace CLOSED\n***** Upcoming Events *****\nSpencer CLOSED\nSanta Rosa 0800 \u2013 1300\nHarold CLOSED\nSite X CLOSED\nChoctaw CLOSED\nSTANDING NOTES:\n1. Snivels shall be in T-SHARP NLT 0800, two working days prior to the date of the snivel. Late snivels require a T-SHARP\nentry followed by verbal notification to the Operations Duty Officer. Late snivels will be handled on a case-by-case basis.\n2. All CAIs and MIL Classes are accessed via T-SHARP: https://tsharp.navsea.cloud.navy.mil . Students are responsible for\nensuring all prerequisite CAIs are completed prior to scheduled events.\n3. All are highly encouraged to complete SAFREP if a notable event occurs: https://saferep.safety.af.mil/\n4. Access publications via Eightball University: https://www.cnatra.navy.mil/tw5/ht8/university.asp or the HT-8 Sharepoint:\nhttps://flankspeed.sharepoint-mil.us/sites/HT-8Main/SitePages/HT8Home.aspx"
    },
    {
      "page": 2,
      "text": "SAFETY OFFICER OPERATIONS OFFICER EXECUTIVE OFFICER COMMANDING OFFICER\nD. MirandaHidalgo, Maj, USMC M. Dominik, LCDR, USNR S. Kohl, CDR, USN D. Burkett, CDR, USN\nFlight (Flight Event) Schedule\nLINE BRIEF SCHD SCHD LNCH LAND INSTRUCTOR STUDENT TYPE SCHD REMARKS\nNUM TIME T/O LAND ICAO ICAO EVENT FLT\nTIME\nT02-1 0800 1015 1351 KNDZ KNDZ Capt ZLOGAR A 1stLt TRULL B TRF4002A 3.6 FLT DOC OBS FOR TSAI\n1stLt OSTI J BI4102A\nLT TSAI E\nT06-1 0800 1015 1403 KNDZ KNDZ LCDR BRAY B 1stLt HOPKINS C TRF4101A 3.8\n1stLt MICO D DAY4502A\nSimulator (Sim Event) Schedule\nLINE BRIEF SCHD SIM/ INSTRUCTOR STUDENT TYPE SCHD REMARKS\nDEVICE\nNUM TIME T/O EVENT TIME\nL7U5-2 0700 0730 L7U5 CIV ASHFORD R LTJG STEVENS E SAR3001A 1.5\nL7U3-2 0700 0730 L7U3 CIV YANNUZZI J LTJG RAUCCI Z SAR3001A 1.5\nL7U2-3 0830 0900 L7U2 CIV HOLLINGER J Capt BENT D TRF3001A 1.5\nL7U12-3 TBD 0900 L7U12 CIV LOEB J LTJG MACKRELL M VIP 1.5 WINGER FAMILY SIM;\nGUESTS: KATHRYN\nMACKRELL, JOHN\nMACKRELL, GRACE\nMACKRELL, LIZA\nMACKRELL, DANIEL\nOFLAHERTY, MARGARET\nGAGLIONE\nL7U6-4 1000 1030 L7U6 CIV ARMSTRONG W 1stLt SLUKA C TRF3001A 1.5\nL7U8-4 TBD 1030 L7U8 CIV CUNNINGHAM G 1stLt FOREMAN A VIP 1.5 WINGER FAMILY SIM;\nGUESTS: YAMA FOREMAN,\nSTEVE FOREMAN, PHILIP\nFOREMAN, PAUL MOORE,\nPRISCILLA MOORE, JENNA\nMOORE, EVA SAVA\nL6U4-4 1000 1030 L6U4 CIV YANNUZZI J 1stLt SCHOFIELD S DAY2002A 1.5\nL7U9-5 1130 1200 L7U9 CIV HAGLUND D LTJG MYHRE S RI3001A 1.5 NET 1130\nL7U12-5 1130 1200 L7U12 CIV RAUSCHER J LTJG GRUENDLING K LND3001A 1.5\nL7U5-6 1300 1330 L7U5 CIV KARR J LTJG MELE J NGT3002A 1.5\nGround Events\nTime Event Location Person Instructor Remarks\nNo Ground Events Scheduled"
